    description: "Finds YouTube topics that already blew up in your niche (read-only). Gathers related channels from seed queries, takes each channel's median views over recent uploads, and counts as outliers only videos at 5x (default) that median or more \u2014 absolute view counts vary with channel size and make a poor yardstick for picking topics. Topic phrases pulled from outlier titles come back as keywords. Take the topics only \u2014 never copy titles, thumbnails, or scripts. With includeComments=true, unresolved questions (unmet needs) mined from top-outlier comments land in gaps. Auth prefers YOUTUBE_API_KEY (spends no publish quota), else channel OAuth youtube.readonly. search.list costs 100 units per call, so at most 4 seeds.",
